{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HxYDgG6WpY3ahmos9SmTnC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '全部四条 Claim 以完整力度着陆。\"31% of MMLU Items Are Functionally Unstable\"\n2\t  作为 discovery paper 被接受。评审认可 \"old psychometric method × unprecedented LLM benchmark\n3\t  scale = genuine empirical discovery\" 的 novelty 逻辑。IRT misspecification（98% |Lz|>2）被视为\n4\t  MMLU 固有多维性的已知现象，作为 honest limitation 处理， 指向 multidimensional IRT future work。\"instability\n5\t  ≠ invalidity\" 叙事清晰，ρ≈0.997 是 strength （massive redundancy），31% 是 diagnostic signal。difficulty×direction\n6\t  ρ=-0.597 作为 mechanistic story 引起共鸣。GSM1K r=-0.478 (N=33) 被视为 suggestive cross-benchmark\n7\t  evidence，宽 CI 被接受为 honest reporting。 reviewer_avg_score: 6.5, acceptance_probability_pct:\n8\t  68, claims_at_full_strength: 4, novelty_sub_score_avg: 3.0, reviewers_flagging_irt_as_fatal:\n9\t  0, major_revisions_needed: 0-1。\n10\t\n11\t  '\n12\timagined_experiments:\n13\t- name: real_data_dif_mmlu\n14\t  plan_id: plan_001\n15\t  description: 'MH-DIF applied to METABENCH MMLU response matrix (5,227 models × 12,508\n16\t    items). Temporal cohort (2023 vs 2024-H1), ability-quintile cohort, within-family\n17\t    confound control, domain-specificity analysis, random-split sanity check.\n18\t\n19\t    '\n20\t  expected_results:\n21\t    temporal_ets_c_pct: 31.3\n22\t    temporal_fpr_li_clean: 0.318\n23\t    temporal_enrichment: 0.96\n24\t    ability_ets_c_pct: 2.9\n25\t    ability_enrichment: 1.19\n26\t    within_family_llama2v3_c_pct: 61.3\n27\t    domain_spearman_rho: 0.307\n28\t    domain_spearman_p: 0.02\n29\t    sanity_random_split_c_pct: 0.18\n30\t    temporal_ability_jaccard: 0.014\n31\t  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，31.3% temporal C% 被评审接受为 genuine empirical discovery——这是首次对\n32\t    LLM benchmark 做如此大规模的 DIF 分析。enrichment≈0.96 不再被解读为 \"DIF 失败\"，而是完美支撑 Claim 2 的\n33\t    meta-critique： Li et al. web-overlap labels 测量的是 global exposure，不是 differential\n34\t    contamination，因此 enrichment≈1.0 是 expected。random split 0.18% 彻底排除统计伪像。domain\n35\t    ρ=0.307 是 modest ecological correlation，但 plan_019 的 item-level decomposition（≤2.4pp/7.6%）证明\n36\t    instability 是 predominantly item-specific，不是 \"models got better\" 的 proxy。评审认可这组结果的\n37\t    completeness 和 methodological rigor（4-way sensitivity matrix + sanity checks）。A1\n38\t    假设成立：ML 评审接受 \"established psychometric method at unprecedented scale\" 的 novelty\n39\t    逻辑。\n40\t\n41\t    '\n42\t  tables:\n43\t  - name: 'Table 1: Temporal DIF Summary'\n44\t    columns:\n45\t    - cohort_definition\n46\t    - N_ref\n47\t    - N_foc\n48\t    - ETS_A_pct\n49\t    - ETS_B_pct\n50\t    - ETS_C_pct\n51\t    - enrichment_vs_Li\n52\t    rows:\n53\t    - - temporal_2023v2024\n54\t      - 1253\n55\t      - 656\n56\t      - 45.2\n57\t      - 23.5\n58\t      - 31.3\n59\t      - 0.96\n60\t    - - ability_quintile\n61\t      - 2613\n62\t      - 2614\n63\t      - 90.8\n64\t      - 6.3\n65\t      - 2.9\n66\t      - 1.19\n67\t    - - random_split_sanity\n68\t      - 2613\n69\t      - 2614\n70\t      - 99.6\n71\t      - 0.2\n72\t      - 0.18\n73\t      - N/A\n74\t  - name: 'Table 2: Domain-Specificity (57 subjects)'\n75\t    columns:\n76\t    - metric\n77\t    - value\n78\t    rows:\n79\t    - - C%_range\n80\t      - 20.7–48.4%\n81\t    - - unweighted_mean\n82\t      - ~30%\n83\t    - - ρ_vs_accuracy_improvement\n84\t      - 0.307\n85\t    - - p_value\n86\t      - 0.02\n87\t  figures_description:\n88\t  - 'Fig 1: Heatmap of 57-subject C% sorted by domain cluster. All subjects show >20%\n89\t    C%. Color gradient from green (20%) to red (48%).'\n90\t  - 'Fig 2: Scatter plot of subject-level C% vs accuracy improvement (ρ=0.307). Modest\n91\t    positive trend, large residual variance emphasizes item-specific drivers.'\n92\t  analysis: 'Plan_001 provides the headline finding. In best tier, the pivot from\n93\t    \"contamination detector\" to \"benchmark characterization\" is complete and compelling.\n94\t    The 31.3% figure survives all robustness checks (plans 018, 019, 020, 022). Within-family\n95\t    Llama-2v3 C%=61.3% is reframed as evidence of genuine capability evolution, not\n96\t    a confound. Two reviewers note the thoroughness of the multi-cohort design; one\n97\t    asks about non-uniform DIF (addressed by plan_021).\n98\t\n99\t    '\n100\t- name: rl_robustness_validation\n101\t  plan_id: plan_002\n102\t  description: 'Validate DIF robustness to RL training: SFT-only baseline, alignment-RL\n103\t    (DPO/ORPO, N=477), 10-15 reasoning-RL models (GRPO/PPO) added to focal cohort.\n104\t    Compare DIF retention vs traditional detector (Min-K%, ConStat) degradation on\n105\t    RL models.\n106\t\n107\t    '\n108\t  expected_results:\n109\t    sft_baseline_c_pct: 30.8\n110\t    alignment_rl_cohort_c_pct: 31.1\n111\t    reasoning_rl_mixed_cohort_c_pct: 30.5\n112\t    jaccard_sft_vs_alignment_rl: 0.89\n113\t    jaccard_sft_vs_reasoning_rl_mixed: 0.86\n114\t    dif_retention_ratio: 0.97\n115\t    constat_auroc_sft: 0.72\n116\t    constat_auroc_reasoning_rl: 0.41\n117\t    mink_auroc_sft: 0.68\n118\t    mink_auroc_reasoning_rl: 0.35\n119\t    tost_equivalence_p: 0.008\n120\t    bootstrap_ci_dif_retention:\n121\t    - 0.93\n122\t    - 1.01\n123\t    n_reasoning_rl_models: 13\n124\t  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，DIF 的 group-level 设计天然免疫 RL。MH-DIF 在 matched-score strata\n125\t    内比较 item 通过率——它不依赖单个模型的 NLL 分布（Min-K%）或 perturbation 响应（ConStat），因此 RL 训练后的 NLL\n126\t    gap contraction 和 generation distribution 变化不影响 DIF。A1 假设成立：评审理解 DIF 是 group-level\n127\t    统计量，13 个 RL 模型混入 ~800+ focal cohort 不会改变 strata 构成。SFT vs alignment-RL Jaccard=0.89\n128\t    反映 DPO/ORPO 不改变 item functioning。ConStat/Min-K% AUROC 从 0.68-0.72 降至 0.35-0.41\n129\t    提供了 explicit contrast。TOST 等价性检验 p=0.008 正式确认 DIF retention。但评审可能注意到 N=13 reasoning-RL\n130\t    太少，最多 1 位评审要求更多模型——在 best 档下这被视为 minor concern 而非 fatal。\n131\t\n132\t    '\n133\t  tables:\n134\t  - name: 'Table S1: DIF Robustness to Training Paradigm'\n135\t    columns:\n136\t    - cohort_composition\n137\t    - N_total\n138\t    - C_pct\n139\t    - Jaccard_vs_SFT\n140\t    - retention_ratio\n141\t    rows:\n142\t    - - SFT_only\n143\t      - 380\n144\t      - 30.8\n145\t      - 1.0\n146\t      - 1.0\n147\t    - - alignment_RL_DPO_ORPO\n148\t      - 477\n149\t      - 31.1\n150\t      - 0.89\n151\t      - 0.97\n152\t    - - mixed_reasoning_RL\n153\t      - 393\n154\t      - 30.5\n155\t      - 0.86\n156\t      - 0.97\n157\t  - name: 'Table S2: Traditional Detector Degradation'\n158\t    columns:\n159\t    - detector\n160\t    - AUROC_SFT\n161\t    - AUROC_reasoning_RL\n162\t    - delta\n163\t    - DeLong_p\n164\t    rows:\n165\t    - - Min-K%\n166\t      - 0.68\n167\t      - 0.35\n168\t      - -0.33\n169\t      - <0.001\n170\t    - - ConStat\n171\t      - 0.72\n172\t      - 0.41\n173\t      - -0.31\n174\t      - <0.001\n175\t    - - DIF_MH\n176\t      - 0.93\n177\t      - 0.91\n178\t      - -0.02\n179\t      - 0.42\n180\t  figures_description:\n181\t  - 'Fig S1: ROC curves for DIF vs Min-K% vs ConStat on SFT cohort (left) and reasoning-RL-mixed\n182\t    cohort (right). DIF curves nearly identical; traditional detectors collapse.'\n183\t  analysis: 'In best tier, this experiment lands as appendix-strength supporting evidence.\n184\t    The N=13 reasoning-RL limitation is acknowledged transparently. The key result\n185\t    is the contrast: traditional detectors degrade dramatically while DIF is invariant.\n186\t    One reviewer may ask whether DIF would still be robust if the focal cohort were\n187\t    majority RL — acknowledged as future work given current reasoning-RL model scarcity.\n188\t    This experiment is NOT in the main body (paper_framing.md already notes N=13 is\n189\t    underpowered → limitations disclosure, not claim).\n190\t\n191\t    '\n192\t- name: constat_perturbation_eval\n193\t  plan_id: plan_003a\n194\t  description: 'Independent ConStat-style perturbation testing on 200+ MMLU items.\n195\t    Generate paraphrases, compare original vs reformulated performance, apply FDR-controlled\n196\t    detection.\n197\t\n198\t    '\n199\t  expected_results:\n200\t    n_items_paraphrased: 250\n201\t    n_models_tested: 15\n202\t    constat_detection_rate_sft: 0.34\n203\t    constat_detection_rate_rl: 0.08\n204\t    fdr_controlled_detections: 62\n205\t    semantic_equivalence_score: 0.91\n206\t    constat_fpr_on_clean: 0.06\n207\t  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，ConStat 在非 RL 模型上展现 moderate detection power（~34%），但在\n208\t    RL 模型上接近 chance level（~8%），验证了 perturbation-based 方法对 RL 的脆弱性。这为 Claim 2 meta-critique\n209\t    提供了 complementary baseline：ConStat 检测的是 verbatim memorization（对 paraphrase 敏感），而非\n210\t    differential contamination。但 paper_framing.md 已将 plan_003a/b/c 标记为 \"never executed,\n211\t    future work\"， 所以即使结果干净，它只出现在 appendix 或 discussion 中作为 \"related method comparison\"。评审不要求\n212\t    这个实验存在——paper 已经 pivoted 到 characterization narrative，不需要 detection method 比较。\n213\t\n214\t    '\n215\t  tables:\n216\t  - name: 'Table S3: ConStat Baseline Performance'\n217\t    columns:\n218\t    - model_type\n219\t    - N_models\n220\t    - detection_rate\n221\t    - FDR_controlled_pct\n222\t    rows:\n223\t    - - SFT\n224\t      - 8\n225\t      - 0.34\n226\t      - 27.2\n227\t    - - DPO/ORPO\n228\t      - 5\n229\t      - 0.21\n230\t      - 14.8\n231\t    - - reasoning_RL\n232\t      - 2\n233\t      - 0.08\n234\t      - 3.2\n235\t  figures_description:\n236\t  - 'Fig S2: Detection rate by model training paradigm showing ConStat degradation\n237\t    under RL.'\n238\t  analysis: 'Dropped from main paper. In best tier, this would have been a clean baseline\n239\t    comparison but is unnecessary for the characterization narrative. If executed,\n240\t    it strengthens the meta-critique (Claim 2) by showing ConStat also can''t distinguish\n241\t    web-overlap from differential contamination. Paper framing correctly categorizes\n242\t    this as future work.\n243\t\n244\t    '\n245\t- name: dvd_generation_variance_eval\n246\t  plan_id: plan_003b\n247\t  description: 'DVD generation variance on MMLU: 10-15 open-weight models, 50 responses\n248\t    per item via temperature sampling, bimodal distribution detection for contamination.\n249\t\n250\t    '\n251\t  expected_results:\n252\t    n_models: 12\n253\t    n_items_tested: 500\n254\t    bimodal_items_detected: 47\n255\t    dvd_auroc_vs_li_labels: 0.58\n256\t    dvd_auroc_vs_semi_synthetic: 0.63\n257\t    variant_contamination_sensitivity: 0.22\n258\t    verbatim_contamination_sensitivity: 0.51\n259\t  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，DVD 展现 moderate verbatim contamination sensitivity（0.51）但\n260\t    variant contamination 几乎无效（0.22）。这是 DVD 方法的 known limitation——generation variance\n261\t    需要 exact memorization 才能产生 bimodal 分布，variant contamination 只改变 posterior probability\n262\t    不产生 bimodality。 与 plan_003a 一样，paper_framing.md 已将其标记为 \"never executed, future\n263\t    work\"。 在 best 档下评审不会因为缺少这个实验而扣分——paper 不声称做 detection method 比较。\n264\t\n265\t    '\n266\t  tables: []\n267\t  figures_description: []\n268\t  analysis: 'Dropped from main paper. Would have provided variant-contamination detection\n269\t    baseline. Paper narrative has pivoted away from detection → characterization,\n270\t    making this unnecessary for acceptance. Best tier does not require execution.\n271\t\n272\t    '\n273\t- name: ensemble_fusion\n274\t  plan_id: plan_003c\n275\t  description: 'Fuse DIF + ConStat + DVD into multi-signal ensemble with calibrated\n276\t    thresholds, majority voting, weighted fusion, and cross-validated weights.\n277\t\n278\t    '\n279\t  expected_results:\n280\t    ensemble_tpr_at_fpr010: 0.78\n281\t    ensemble_coverage_complementarity: 0.89\n282\t    dif_unique_detections_pct: 31\n283\t    constat_unique_detections_pct: 18\n284\t    dvd_unique_detections_pct: 7\n285\t    overlap_all_three_pct: 12\n286\t    fusion_auroc: 0.82\n287\t    uniform_weight_auroc: 0.79\n288\t  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，三信号 ensemble 理论上能覆盖更多 contamination 类型（DIF: differential,\n289\t    ConStat: verbatim, DVD: bimodal），但 paper_framing.md 明确将其标记为 \"never executed, future\n290\t    work\"。 Paper 已从 \"detection ensemble\" 彻底转向 \"characterization + meta-critique\"。\n291\t    评审不会因为没有 ensemble 而降分——paper 的 novelty 来自 scale + meta-critique + framework，不是更好的检测器。\n292\t\n293\t    '\n294\t  tables: []\n295\t  figures_description: []\n296\t  analysis: 'Explicitly dropped. Not needed for best-tier acceptance under the current\n297\t    characterization framing. Would only matter if the paper claimed to build a better\n298\t    contamination detector, which it does not.\n299\t\n300\t    '\n301\t- name: cross_benchmark_gsm8k\n302\t  plan_id: plan_004\n303\t  description: 'Three-step GSM8K replication: (1) temporal DIF on 1,319 items × 6,702\n304\t    models, (2) semi-synthetic injection validation, (3) GSM1K contamination gap correlation\n305\t    (N=33).\n306\t\n307\t    '\n308\t  expected_results:\n309\t    step1_temporal_c_pct: 18.9\n310\t    step1_sanity_c_pct: 0.3\n311\t    step2_standard_delta_tpr_p10: 0.818\n312\t    step2_external_delta_tpr_p10: 0.517\n313\t    step3_pearson_r: -0.478\n314\t    step3_pearson_p: 0.005\n315\t    step3_spearman_rho: -0.403\n316\t    step3_spearman_p: 0.02\n317\t    step3_partial_r: -0.385\n318\t    step3_partial_p: 0.027\n319\t    step3_permutation_p: 0.014\n320\t    step3_n_models: 33\n321\t    step3_bca_ci_pearson:\n322\t    - -0.714\n323\t    - -0.155\n324\t    step3_bca_ci_spearman:\n325\t    - -0.687\n326\t    - -0.031\n327\t    step3_leave_one_out_r_range:\n328\t    - -0.537\n329\t    - -0.374\n330\t  result_rationale: 'Best 档下 A6 假设成立：GSM1K r=-0.478 (N=33) 被视为 suggestive cross-benchmark\n331\t    evidence。 所有 CI 排除零。方向是 NEGATIVE（opposite to naive contamination hypothesis），但\n332\t    best 档下评审 接受论文的解读：DIF-C items 抵抗 contamination-based gains，contamination 产生的 surface-level\n333\t    improvement 集中在 non-DIF items。宽 CI（Pearson upper bound |r|=0.155, Spearman upper\n334\t    bound near zero）被视为 honest reporting 而非 weakness。Leave-one-out stability 和 partial\n335\t    r 控制 overall accuracy 加分。至少 2/3 评审认为 N=33 sufficient for \"suggestive\" claim，不要求\n336\t    \"definitive\"。Cook''s d 分析排除单一 outlier 驱动。这是 Claim 4 的第四层 sub-finding， 不是 standalone\n337\t    claim——评审评价时将其视为 complementary evidence，不对其 standalone significance 设高标准。\n338\t\n339\t    '\n340\t  tables:\n341\t  - name: 'Table 4: GSM1K Contamination Gap Correlation'\n342\t    columns:\n343\t    - method\n344\t    - statistic\n345\t    - value\n346\t    - p_value\n347\t    - 95%_BCa_CI\n348\t    rows:\n349\t    - - Pearson\n350\t      - r\n351\t      - -0.478\n352\t      - 0.005\n353\t      - '[-0.714, -0.155]'\n354\t    - - Spearman\n355\t      - ρ\n356\t      - -0.403\n357\t      - 0.02\n358\t      - '[-0.687, -0.031]'\n359\t    - - Partial_r\n360\t      - r_partial\n361\t      - -0.385\n362\t      - 0.027\n363\t      - '[-0.640, -0.058]'\n364\t    - - Permutation\n365\t      - p_perm\n366\t      - N/A\n367\t      - 0.014\n368\t      - N/A\n369\t  - name: 'Table 3: GSM8K Temporal DIF'\n370\t    columns:\n371\t    - metric\n372\t    - standard_MH\n373\t    - external_MH\n374\t    - sanity\n375\t    rows:\n376\t    - - C_pct\n377\t      - 18.9\n378\t      - 47.4\n379\t      - 0.3\n380\t    - - N_ref\n381\t      - 1017\n382\t      - 1017\n383\t      - 3350\n384\t    - - N_foc\n385\t      - 804\n386\t      - 804\n387\t      - 3352\n388\t    - - ΔTPR_p10\n389\t      - 0.818\n390\t      - 0.517\n391\t      - N/A\n392\t  figures_description:\n393\t  - 'Fig 4: Scatter plot of model-level GSM1K contamination gap vs DIF-C item accuracy\n394\t    gap. r=-0.478, regression line with BCa CI band. Deepseek-math-7b-rl labeled as\n395\t    Cook''s d max.'\n396\t  - 'Fig S3: GSM8K dose-response curve (ΔTPR vs injection probability p) for standard\n397\t    and external MH variants.'\n398\t  analysis: 'In best tier, Step 3 is the key value-add: cross-benchmark evidence that\n399\t    DIF items resist contamination-based gains. The negative direction is the surprise\n400\t    finding that elevates the paper — it''s not what a naive contamination-detection\n401\t    paper would predict, but perfectly consistent with the characterization narrative.\n402\t    Step 1 (C%=18.9%) confirms temporal DIF generalizes beyond MMLU. Step 2 (ΔTPR=0.818)\n403\t    confirms the semi-synthetic framework is portable. Reviewers appreciate the multi-step\n404\t    validation chain. One reviewer may note the wide CI and small N, but in best tier\n405\t    this is flagged as \"appropriately caveated.\"\n406\t\n407\t    '\n408\t- name: bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\n409\t  plan_id: plan_005\n410\t  description: 'Bifactor IRT (1 general + 57 subject-specific factors) equating pilot.\n411\t    Killed after plan_014 pre-check showed within-subject C%=38.1%.\n412\t\n413\t    '\n414\t  expected_results:\n415\t    status: killed\n416\t    kill_reason: 'plan_014 pre-check: within-subject C%=38.1% (>25%), proving temporal\n417\t      DIF penetrates subject level'\n418\t    bifactor_would_have_achieved: At best marginal FPR reduction from 31% to ~27%,\n419\t      insufficient to justify complexity\n420\t  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，bifactor kill 是 methodological honesty 的正面信号。评审看到的叙事是：\n421\t    \"We tried three structural improvements (matched ability, θ-conditioning, bifactor\n422\t    pre-check), all failed to reduce baseline FPR → this is an empirical observation\n423\t    about the nature of temporal DIF in LLM benchmarks, not a fixable methodological\n424\t    limitation.\" A2 假设成立： 评审将 98% |Lz|>2 + bifactor failure 解读为 MMLU 固有多维性的已知现象。Limitations\n425\t    中用 1-2 段 坦承即可，指向 multidimensional IRT future work。评审赞赏 \"we tried it, it didn''t\n426\t    work, here''s what that tells us\" 的研究诚实性。\n427\t\n428\t    '\n429\t  tables: []\n430\t  figures_description: []\n431\t  analysis: 'Killed experiment. In best tier, the killing is itself evidence — it\n432\t    contributes to the \"empirical observation of structural constraints\" narrative\n433\t    in §5 Discussion. No reviewer penalizes a well-documented null result that motivates\n434\t    future work.\n435\t\n436\t    '\n437\t- name: item_generation_calibration\n438\t  plan_id: plan_006\n439\t  description: 'Generate replacement items for DIF-flagged MMLU questions via LLM\n440\t    generation with construct constraints + student simulation calibration.\n441\t\n442\t    '\n443\t  expected_results:\n444\t    status: not_executed\n445\t    reason: Depends on plan_005 (bifactor) which was killed. Item generation without\n446\t      equating framework has no anchor.\n447\t    hypothetical_difficulty_correlation_prompt: 0.28\n448\t    hypothetical_difficulty_correlation_simulation: 0.71\n449\t  result_rationale: 'Best 档下不需要这个实验。Paper 已从 \"regeneration\" 彻底 pivot 到 \"characterization\"。\n450\t    Claim 3 是 semi-synthetic validation framework，不是 item replacement pipeline。 评审不会要求\n451\t    item generation 因为 paper 不声称解决 benchmark repair 问题——它声称提供 diagnostic lens。即使存在\n452\t    regeneration 结果也会放 appendix。\n453\t\n454\t    '\n455\t  tables: []\n456\t  figures_description: []\n457\t  analysis: 'Dependency killed. Not needed for any of the 4 current claims. Paper''s\n458\t    scope control explicitly excludes regeneration from main body.\n459\t\n460\t    '\n461\t- name: cumulative_bayesian_dif\n462\t  plan_id: plan_007\n463\t  description: 'Bayesian DIF priors (Sinharay et al., 2006) across 4 simulated successive\n464\t    administrations. Show power improvement from cumulative evidence.\n465\t\n466\t    '\n467\t  expected_results:\n468\t    single_admin_power_delta10: 0.42\n469\t    cumulative_2admin_power: 0.58\n470\t    cumulative_3admin_power: 0.71\n471\t    cumulative_4admin_power: 0.79\n472\t    bayes_factor_threshold: 3.0\n473\t    fpr_cumulative: 0.038\n474\t  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，cumulative Bayesian DIF 在 simulation 层面展现 clean power\n475\t    improvement (0.42→0.79 over 4 administrations)，验证 longitudinal monitoring 理论可行性。\n476\t    但 paper_framing.md 已将其标记为 \"simulation-only, underdeveloped\"，放 appendix。 评审不对 appendix\n477\t    材料严格评审。在 best 档下，有 1 位评审可能在 \"interesting future direction\" 中提到这个结果，但不会影响分数。A3\n478\t    假设的 \"instability ≠ invalidity\" 叙事不依赖此实验。\n479\t\n480\t    '\n481\t  tables:\n482\t  - name: 'Table S4: Cumulative Bayesian DIF Power'\n483\t    columns:\n484\t    - n_administrations\n485\t    - power_delta10\n486\t    - power_delta14\n487\t    - FPR\n488\t    rows:\n489\t    - - 1\n490\t      - 0.42\n491\t      - 0.68\n492\t      - 0.041\n493\t    - - 2\n494\t      - 0.58\n495\t      - 0.82\n496\t      - 0.039\n497\t    - - 3\n498\t      - 0.71\n499\t      - 0.91\n500\t      - 0.037\n501\t    - - 4\n502\t      - 0.79\n503\t      - 0.95\n504\t      - 0.038\n505\t  figures_description:\n506\t  - 'Fig S4: Power accumulation curve across successive administrations for δ=1.0\n507\t    and δ=1.4.'\n508\t  analysis: 'Appendix-only. Clean simulation result but not load-bearing for any claim.\n509\t    Best tier treats this as \"bonus content that signals the authors thought ahead\"\n510\t    without affecting the acceptance decision.\n511\t\n512\t    '\n513\t- name: graceful_degradation_analysis\n514\t  plan_id: plan_008\n515\t  description: 'Formal analysis of benchmark validity under progressive item replacement\n516\t    (5%, 10%, 20%, 50%). Define validity metrics, simulate degradation, establish\n517\t    theoretical bounds.\n518\t\n519\t    '\n520\t  expected_results:\n521\t    rho_at_5pct_replacement: 0.999\n522\t    rho_at_10pct_replacement: 0.997\n523\t    rho_at_20pct_replacement: 0.993\n524\t    rho_at_50pct_replacement: 0.975\n525\t    reliability_alpha_full: 0.962\n526\t    reliability_alpha_50pct_replaced: 0.948\n527\t    construct_coverage_loss_at_20pct: 0.03\n528\t  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，graceful degradation 直接支持 \"instability ≠ invalidity\"\n529\t    叙事：即使替换 50% items，ρ=0.975 且 reliability 仅降 0.014。但 paper_framing.md 将其标记为 supplementary，\n530\t    depends on plan_005+006 which were killed。在 best 档下，plan_017 的 ρ≈0.997（DIF removal）\n531\t    已经提供了等价的 evidence——graceful degradation 是 plan_017 的理论扩展，非必需。 即使不执行，Claim 4 的\n532\t    redundancy sub-finding (ρ≈0.997) 已经 cover 了这个角度。\n533\t\n534\t    '\n535\t  tables: []\n536\t  figures_description: []\n537\t  analysis: 'Dependency killed (plan_005/006). Effectively replaced by plan_017''s\n538\t    empirical ρ≈0.997 result. In best tier, plan_017 alone is sufficient for the redundancy\n539\t    argument.\n540\t\n541\t    '\n542\t- name: item_focused_trees\n543\t  plan_id: plan_009\n544\t  description: 'Item-Focused Trees (Tutz & Berger, 2016) treating model release date\n545\t    as continuous covariate. Alternative to categorical cohort DIF.\n546\t\n547\t    '\n548\t  expected_results:\n549\t    ift_flagged_items_pct: 28.7\n550\t    ift_mh_concordance_jaccard: 0.72\n551\t    ift_unique_detections: 412\n552\t    mh_unique_detections: 738\n553\t    ift_mh_overlap: 3180\n554\t    continuous_date_splitting_r2: 0.31\n555\t    ift_avoids_arbitrary_cutoff: true\n556\t  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，IFT 作为 robustness check 展现 moderate concordance with\n557\t    MH (Jaccard=0.72)。 28.7% flagged items 接近 MH 的 31.3%，确认 temporal instability 不是\n558\t    arbitrary cohort split 的产物。IFT 特有检测 (412 items) 反映 continuous temporal trends\n559\t    而非 abrupt regime changes。 paper_framing.md 标记为 appendix robustness check。评审可能\n560\t    appreciate 但不影响分数。\n561\t\n562\t    '\n563\t  tables:\n564\t  - name: 'Table S5: IFT vs MH Concordance'\n565\t    columns:\n566\t    - method\n567\t    - items_flagged\n568\t    - overlap_with_MH\n569\t    - unique_detections\n570\t    - Jaccard\n571\t    rows:\n572\t    - - MH_DIF\n573\t      - 3918\n574\t      - 3180\n575\t      - 738\n576\t      - —\n577\t    - - IFT\n578\t      - 3592\n579\t      - 3180\n580\t      - 412\n581\t      - 0.72\n582\t  figures_description:\n583\t  - 'Fig S5: Release-date splits from IFT for 6 example items, showing continuous\n584\t    DIF trajectories vs MH binary classification.'\n585\t  analysis: 'Appendix robustness check. In best tier, confirms MH findings are not\n586\t    artifacts of the 2023/2024 binary split. Clean supplementary evidence.\n587\t\n588\t    '\n589\t- name: architecture_stratified_dif\n590\t  plan_id: plan_010\n591\t  description: 'DIF within decoder-only models only (99.98% of METABENCH MMLU). Report\n592\t    IRT fit diagnostics, compare C% vs full population.\n593\t\n594\t    '\n595\t  expected_results:\n596\t    decoder_only_pct: 99.98\n597\t    decoder_only_n: 5226\n598\t    non_decoder_n: 1\n599\t    c_pct_decoder_only: 31.3\n600\t    c_pct_full: 31.3\n601\t    jaccard_decoder_vs_full: 1.0\n602\t    irt_fit_unchanged: true\n603\t  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，这个实验的结论极为干净：METABENCH MMLU 中 5226/5227 模型是 decoder-only，\n604\t    排除 1 个 non-decoder 模型后 C% 完全不变 (Jaccard=1.0)。这彻底消除 \"architecture heterogeneity\n605\t    causes spurious DIF\" 的 concern。评审看到 99.98% homogeneity 后不会再追问 architecture confound。\n606\t    A2 假设强化：98% |Lz|>2 不是 architecture mixing 导致的，而是 MMLU 57-subject 多维性的固有属性。 这是\n607\t    proactive defense 的典范——Dream worst-case 识别的 concern 在实际数据中根本不存在。\n608\t\n609\t    '\n610\t  tables:\n611\t  - name: 'Table S6: Architecture Composition'\n612\t    columns:\n613\t    - architecture\n614\t    - N\n615\t    - pct\n616\t    - C_pct_within\n617\t    rows:\n618\t    - - decoder_only\n619\t      - 5226\n620\t      - 99.98\n621\t      - 31.3\n622\t    - - non_decoder\n623\t      - 1\n624\t      - 0.02\n625\t      - N/A (excluded)\n626\t    - - full_population\n627\t      - 5227\n628\t      - 100\n629\t      - 31.3\n630\t  figures_description: []\n631\t  analysis: 'Decisive negative result that kills the architecture confound concern\n632\t    in one number. In best tier, this appears in §4.1 as a single sentence: \"METABENCH\n633\t    MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5,226/5,227); excluding the single non-decoder model\n634\t    changes nothing (Jaccard=1.0).\" Reviewers appreciate the thoroughness of checking.\n635\t\n636\t    '\n637\t- name: semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\n638\t  plan_id: plan_011\n639\t  description: 'Inject known differential contamination into real METABENCH response\n640\t    matrix. Measure DIF detection power (TPR/FPR) under controlled ground truth at\n641\t    varying injection rates.\n642\t\n643\t    '\n644\t  expected_results:\n645\t    temporal_external_tpr_p0: 0.326\n646\t    temporal_external_tpr_p03: 0.548\n647\t    temporal_external_tpr_p05: 0.834\n648\t    temporal_external_tpr_p07: 0.99\n649\t    temporal_external_tpr_p10: 1.0\n650\t    temporal_external_fpr: 0.314\n651\t    temporal_external_delta_tpr_p05: 0.508\n652\t    temporal_external_delta_tpr_p10: 0.674\n653\t    dose_response_monotonic: true\n654\t    matching_variable_contamination_confirmed: true\n655\t    standard_mh_fpr_inflation_at_p10: 0.298→0.616\n656\t  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，semi-synthetic injection 是 Claim 3 的核心 evidence。ΔTPR=+0.508\n657\t    at p=0.5 证明 DIF 确实能检测 differential contamination（不只是 capability improvement）。\n658\t    清晰的 dose-response curve (p=0.3→0.5→0.7→1.0) 展现 power 随 contamination severity\n659\t    单调递增。FPR=0.314 不变证明 injection 不 inflate false positives（用 external matching variant）。\n660\t    Standard MH 的 FPR inflation (0.298→0.616) 暴露了 matching variable contamination\n661\t    问题—— 这 motivates plan_016 的 cross-subject matching solution。评审认可 \"inject into\n662\t    real matrices, not simulated\" 的方法论选择。A4 假设部分成立：semi-synthetic framework 是 reusable\n663\t    infrastructure contribution，2/3 评审视其为 non-obvious methodological innovation。\n664\t\n665\t    '\n666\t  tables:\n667\t  - name: 'Table 5: Semi-Synthetic Injection Results (External MH)'\n668\t    columns:\n669\t    - injection_rate_p\n670\t    - TPR\n671\t    - FPR\n672\t    - ΔTPR\n673\t    rows:\n674\t    - - 0.0_baseline\n675\t      - 0.326\n676\t      - 0.314\n677\t      - —\n678\t    - - 0.3\n679\t      - 0.548\n680\t      - 0.314\n681\t      - 0.222\n682\t    - - 0.5\n683\t      - 0.834\n684\t      - 0.314\n685\t      - 0.508\n686\t    - - 0.7\n687\t      - 0.99\n688\t      - 0.314\n689\t      - 0.664\n690\t    - - 1.0\n691\t      - 1.0\n692\t      - 0.314\n693\t      - 0.674\n694\t  figures_description:\n695\t  - 'Fig 3: Dose-response curve showing TPR vs injection probability p for external\n696\t    MH. Monotonic increase with plateau at p≥0.7. FPR line flat at 0.314.'\n697\t  - 'Fig S6: Comparison of standard MH (FPR inflates) vs external MH (FPR stable)\n698\t    under injection, demonstrating matching variable contamination effect.'\n699\t  analysis: 'Load-bearing evidence for Claim 3. In best tier, the dose-response monotonicity\n700\t    and FPR stability are the two key properties reviewers care about. The matching\n701\t    variable contamination discovery (standard MH FPR inflates) adds methodological\n702\t    depth — it''s the kind of finding that makes reviewers trust the authors understand\n703\t    their method deeply. Cross-subject matching solution (plan_016 ΔFPR=0.000) completes\n704\t    the story.\n705\t\n706\t    '\n707\t- name: threshold_sensitivity\n708\t  plan_id: plan_018\n709\t  description: 'ETS threshold robustness: C% at |Δ_MH| thresholds {1.0, 1.5, 2.0,\n710\t    2.5}. BH FDR correction at q=0.05. Random-split sanity check.\n711\t\n712\t    '\n713\t  expected_results:\n714\t    c_pct_threshold_1_0: 48.9\n715\t    c_pct_threshold_1_5: 31.3\n716\t    c_pct_threshold_2_0: 18.3\n717\t    c_pct_threshold_2_5: 10.2\n718\t    bh_fdr_items_removed: 3\n719\t    bh_fdr_c_pct_after: 31.3\n720\t    bh_impact_negligible: true\n721\t    finding_above_15pct_at_standard_thresholds: true\n722\t    finding_above_10pct_at_conservative: true\n723\t  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，threshold sensitivity 是 Claim 1 最强的 robustness evidence\n724\t    之一。C% 从 48.9% (liberal) 到 10.2% (most conservative) 的 monotonic decline 展现 finding\n725\t    的 gradient nature—— 不是 binary threshold artifact。即使在最保守的 |Δ_MH|≥2.5 下仍有 10.2%\n726\t    (1,278 items) 展现 large DIF。BH FDR 只移除 3/3,918 items 证明 ETS 双重要求（effect size +\n727\t    significance） 提供了几乎完整的隐式多重检验保护。A3 假设成立：评审接受 \"finding is robust across standard\n728\t    thresholds\" 的 framing。诚实地报告 2.5 threshold 低于 15% 加分——shows intellectual honesty。\n729\t\n730\t    '\n731\t  tables:\n732\t  - name: 'Table 2: Threshold Sensitivity Analysis'\n733\t    columns:\n734\t    - '|Δ_MH|_threshold'\n735\t    - ETS_class\n736\t    - C_pct\n737\t    - N_items\n738\t    - BH_impact\n739\t    rows:\n740\t    - - ≥1.0\n741\t      - C\n742\t      - 48.9\n743\t      - 6109\n744\t      - 0 removed\n745\t    - - ≥1.5\n746\t      - C\n747\t      - 31.3\n748\t      - 3918\n749\t      - 3 removed (→31.30%)\n750\t    - - ≥2.0\n751\t      - extreme_C\n752\t      - 18.3\n753\t      - 2288\n754\t      - 0 removed\n755\t    - - ≥2.5\n756\t      - extreme_C\n757\t      - 10.2\n758\t      - 1278\n759\t      - 0 removed\n760\t  figures_description:\n761\t  - 'Fig 2b: Bar chart of C% across 4 thresholds with BH-corrected overlay (nearly\n762\t    invisible reduction).'\n763\t  analysis: 'Essential robustness for Claim 1. In best tier, the clean monotonic gradient\n764\t    and BH near-zero impact are exactly what reviewers want to see. This pre-empts\n765\t    concern #7 (ETS threshold uncalibrated) and concern #8 (multiple testing) simultaneously.\n766\t\n767\t    '\n768\t- name: instability_decomposition\n769\t  plan_id: plan_019\n770\t  description: 'Decompose temporal DIF into domain capability improvement vs item-specific\n771\t    instability. Subject-level ecological correlation vs item-level logistic model.\n772\t\n773\t    '\n774\t  expected_results:\n775\t    subject_level_rho: 0.307\n776\t    subject_level_p: 0.02\n777\t    item_level_pseudo_r2: 0.0007\n778\t    domain_improvement_contribution_pp: 2.4\n779\t    domain_improvement_contribution_pct: 7.6\n780\t    model1_primary: true\n781\t    model2_simpson_supplementary: true\n782\t  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，plan_019 是对 \"38% could just mean models got better\" concern\n783\t    的决定性回应。 Subject-level ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) 是 modest ecological correlation，但 item-level\n784\t    decomposition 展现 pseudo R²=0.0007——domain improvement 只解释 2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%)。这证明\n785\t    instability 是 predominantly item-specific，不是 capability improvement 的 proxy。 A5\n786\t    假设成立（与 plan_023 联合）：difficulty×direction ρ=-0.597 提供了 mechanistic story—— capability\n787\t    improvement concentrates on hard items，而 easy items 的 difficulty structure erodes。评审接受\n788\t    \"ecological correlation grossly overstates item-level relationship\" 的 statistical\n789\t    reasoning。Model 1 vs Model 2 区分（confounder vs mediator）展现 methodological sophistication。\n790\t\n791\t    '\n792\t  tables:\n793\t  - name: 'Table S7: Instability Decomposition'\n794\t    columns:\n795\t    - level\n796\t    - metric\n797\t    - value\n798\t    - interpretation\n799\t    rows:\n800\t    - - subject_level\n801\t      - Spearman_ρ\n802\t      - 0.307\n803\t      - modest ecological correlation\n804\t    - - subject_level\n805\t      - p_value\n806\t      - 0.02\n807\t      - significant but weak\n808\t    - - item_level\n809\t      - pseudo_R²\n810\t      - 0.0007\n811\t      - domain improvement explains <1% variance\n812\t    - - item_level\n813\t      - contribution_pp\n814\t      - 2.4\n815\t      - of 31.3% C%, only 2.4pp from domain improvement\n816\t    - - item_level\n817\t      - contribution_pct\n818\t      - 7.6\n819\t      - 92.4% of instability is item-specific\n820\t  figures_description:\n821\t  - 'Fig S7: Left: subject-level ρ=0.307 scatter. Right: item-level decomposition\n822\t    showing 92.4% item-specific vs 7.6% domain-explained.'\n823\t  analysis: 'Resolves anticipated concern #1 definitively. In best tier, the two-level\n824\t    analysis (ecological vs item-level) is exactly the methodological sophistication\n825\t    reviewers expect. The 7.6% figure becomes a key talking point: \"less than 8% of\n826\t    temporal instability can be attributed to models getting better.\"\n827\t\n828\t    '\n829\t- name: circularity_ablation\n830\t  plan_id: plan_020\n831\t  description: 'Compare DIF removal disruption vs alternative item selection heuristics\n832\t    (accuracy-gap, high-variance, high-discrimination, random). Test whether DIF''s\n833\t    ranking disruption result is tautological.\n834\t\n835\t    '\n836\t  expected_results:\n837\t    dif_removal_z: -9.5\n838\t    accuracy_gap_removal_z: -157\n839\t    high_variance_removal_z: -108\n840\t    high_discrimination_removal_z: -16\n841\t    random_removal_z: 0\n842\t    dif_vs_accgap_ratio: 16×_less_disruptive\n843\t    dif_vs_disc_ratio: 1.7×_less_disruptive\n844\t    dif_accgap_item_overlap_pct: 62.6\n845\t    dif_disc_jaccard: 0.12\n846\t    dif_disc_overlap_pct: 22.1\n847\t    dif_rho_2024: 0.997\n848\t  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，circularity ablation 是 Claim 4 中最精巧的分析。尽管 DIF 和 accuracy-gap\n849\t    selection 有 62.6% item overlap，MH 的 ability conditioning 使 DIF removal 的 disruption\n850\t    小 16 倍 (z=-9.5 vs z=-157)。这证明 MH 不是在找 \"大 accuracy gap\" items——它在控制能力后隔离了 genuine\n851\t    differential functioning。DIF-discrimination overlap 仅 22.1% (Jaccard=0.12) 证明\n852\t    DIF identifies \"items that changed across generations\" 而非 \"good items\"。 评审 concern\n853\t    #11 (tautology) 被彻底 refuted。A3 假设强化：DIF removal 仍然比 random 显著 (z=-9.5)，但远小于 naive\n854\t    heuristics——这就是 \"DIF items carry signal but are NOT the most ranking-defining\n855\t    items\" 的 precise meaning。\n856\t\n857\t    '\n858\t  tables:\n859\t  - name: 'Table 6: Circularity Ablation (Ranking Disruption by Removal Strategy)'\n860\t    columns:\n861\t    - strategy\n862\t    - n_items\n863\t    - ρ_full_vs_subset\n864\t    - disruption_z\n865\t    - overlap_with_DIF_pct\n866\t    rows:\n867\t    - - random_baseline\n868\t      - 3918\n869\t      - 0.9985\n870\t      - 0\n871\t      - —\n872\t    - - DIF_C_removal\n873\t      - 3918\n874\t      - 0.997\n875\t      - -9.5\n876\t      - 100\n877\t    - - high_discrimination\n878\t      - 3918\n879\t      - 0.9958\n880\t      - -16\n881\t      - 22.1\n882\t    - - high_variance\n883\t      - 3918\n884\t      - 0.9831\n885\t      - -108\n886\t      - 41.3\n887\t    - - accuracy_gap\n888\t      - 3918\n889\t      - 0.9712\n890\t      - -157\n891\t      - 62.6\n892\t  figures_description:\n893\t  - 'Fig 5: Bar chart of disruption z-scores by removal strategy. DIF is closest to\n894\t    random despite 62.6% overlap with accuracy-gap. Demonstrates MH conditioning effect.'\n895\t  analysis: 'Key evidence for Claim 4 sub-finding 2. In best tier, this analysis demonstrates\n896\t    deep methodological understanding. The 62.6% overlap + 16× disruption gap is the\n897\t    \"aha moment\" that convinces reviewers MH-DIF is doing something genuinely different\n898\t    from naive accuracy comparison. Tautology concern fully resolved.\n899\t\n900\t    '\n901\t- name: nonuniform_dif_robustness\n902\t  plan_id: plan_021\n903\t  description: 'Logistic Regression DIF on 9 subjects (1,787 items). Test MH''s uniform-only\n904\t    assumption and quantify non-uniform DIF prevalence.\n905\t\n906\t    '\n907\t  expected_results:\n908\t    n_subjects: 9\n909\t    n_items: 1787\n910\t    mh_lr_concordance: 0.921\n911\t    nonuniform_dif_significance_pct: 38.7\n912\t    nonuniform_dif_effect_size_pct: 24.8\n913\t    mh_conservative_estimate_confirmed: true\n914\t  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，LR-DIF 的 92.1% concordance with MH 证明 MH classification\n915\t    对 uniform DIF 是 robust。38.7% non-uniform DIF at significance threshold, 24.8%\n916\t    at |β_interaction|≥0.5 证明 MH 结构性地 underestimates instability——31% 是 conservative\n917\t    estimate。 评审 concern #9 (only uniform DIF) 被直接回应：\"our 31% uniform-only estimate\n918\t    is conservative; including non-uniform DIF raises it to ~25% additional items.\"\n919\t    Best 档下评审接受 caveat (LR used within-subject matching vs MH''s cross-benchmark)\n920\t    并同意使用 24.8% (effect-size controlled) 而非 38.7% (significance-only)。这展现方法论 conservatism。\n921\t\n922\t    '\n923\t  tables:\n924\t  - name: 'Table S8: Non-Uniform DIF (Logistic Regression)'\n925\t    columns:\n926\t    - metric\n927\t    - value\n928\t    rows:\n929\t    - - MH_LR_C_concordance\n930\t      - 92.1%\n931\t    - - non_uniform_DIF_significance\n932\t      - 38.7%\n933\t    - - non_uniform_DIF_effect_size\n934\t      - 24.8% (|β_int|≥0.5)\n935\t    - - n_subjects_tested\n936\t      - 9\n937\t    - - n_items_tested\n938\t      - 1787\n939\t  figures_description:\n940\t  - 'Fig S8: MH classification vs LR classification confusion matrix. 92.1% concordance\n941\t    for ETS C class.'\n942\t  analysis: 'Appendix robustness check. In best tier, the key message is \"31% is conservative\"\n943\t    — this flips a potential weakness (MH is old/simple) into a strength (our estimate\n944\t    is a lower bound). The 24.8% effect-size-controlled figure is the one used in\n945\t    the paper text.\n946\t\n947\t    '\n948\t- name: model_independence\n949\t  plan_id: plan_022\n950\t  description: 'Graduated de-duplication: cap models per family at K={1,2,5,10,20}.\n951\t    Compare C% at each cap vs random subsample of same size. Test whether family structure\n952\t    inflates DIF.\n953\t\n954\t    '\n955\t  expected_results:\n956\t    k20_n_models: 447\n957\t    k20_c_pct: 29.1\n958\t    k20_random_c_pct: 30.9\n959\t    k10_c_pct: 24.3\n960\t    k10_random_c_pct: 27.5\n961\t    k5_n_models: 146\n962\t    k5_c_pct: 11.7\n963\t    k5_random_c_pct: 16.9\n964\t    k1_n_models: 33\n965\t    k1_c_pct: 0.17\n966\t    k1_note: underpowered (N<80)\n967\t    family_inflates_c_pct: false\n968\t    dif_at_every_cap_leq_random: true\n969\t  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，graduated de-duplication 是对 concern #10 (model non-independence)\n970\t    的决定性回应。 在每个 cap K 下，family-capped C% ≤ random subsample C%。K=20: 29.1% vs 30.9%,\n971\t    K=5: 11.7% vs 16.9%。Family structure 不仅不 inflate C%，反而 slightly reduces it。 K=1\n972\t    (33 families) 的 0.17% 是 underpowered (N<80) 导致 MH test 无法达到 significance， 不是 DIF\n973\t    消失。评审接受 graduated design 的 methodological rigor——不是 cherry-pick 一个 K， 而是 show\n974\t    monotonic trend。A1 假设强化：31.3% 是 genuine 的，not an artifact of model duplication。\n975\t\n976\t    '\n977\t  tables:\n978\t  - name: 'Table S9: Model Independence — Graduated De-duplication'\n979\t    columns:\n980\t    - cap_K\n981\t    - N_models\n982\t    - C_pct_family_cap\n983\t    - C_pct_random_subsample\n984\t    - delta\n985\t    rows:\n986\t    - - 20\n987\t      - 447\n988\t      - 29.1\n989\t      - 30.9\n990\t      - -1.8\n991\t    - - 10\n992\t      - 283\n993\t      - 24.3\n994\t      - 27.5\n995\t      - -3.2\n996\t    - - 5\n997\t      - 146\n998\t      - 11.7\n999\t      - 16.9\n1000\t      - -5.2\n1001\t    - - 2\n1002\t      - 66\n1003\t      - 2.1\n1004\t      - 5.8\n1005\t      - -3.7\n1006\t    - - 1\n1007\t      - 33\n1008\t      - 0.17\n1009\t      - 0.84\n1010\t      - -0.67 (underpowered)\n1011\t  figures_description:\n1012\t  - 'Fig S9: Paired line plot of C% (family-capped vs random subsample) at each K.\n1013\t    Family-capped consistently at or below random.'\n1014\t  analysis: 'Resolves concern #10. In best tier, the graduated design is elegant —\n1015\t    it shows the relationship between sample independence and DIF detection is not\n1016\t    driven by model family inflation. The \"family C% ≤ random C%\" pattern at every\n1017\t    K is stronger than just showing \"similar\" — it shows family structure, if anything,\n1018\t    suppresses DIF detection.\n1019\t\n1020\t    '\n1021\t- name: item_characterization\n1022\t  plan_id: plan_023\n1023\t  description: 'Characterize DIF-C items by difficulty, discrimination, domain distribution,\n1024\t    and DIF direction. Key finding: difficulty×direction interaction.\n1025\t\n1026\t    '\n1027\t  expected_results:\n1028\t    difficulty_cohen_d: -0.247\n1029\t    discrimination_cohen_d: 0.23\n1030\t    domain_chi2_p: 0.32\n1031\t    domain_uniformly_distributed: true\n1032\t    direction_focal_favoring_pct: 43.9\n1033\t    direction_reference_favoring_pct: 56.1\n1034\t    difficulty_direction_rho: -0.597\n1035\t    hardest_decile_focal_favoring_pct: 88.7\n1036\t    easiest_decile_reference_favoring_pct: 96.2\n1037\t  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，plan_023 是 Claim 4 的 surprise finding 升华全文。difficulty×direction\n1038\t    ρ=-0.597 揭示了一个系统性 pattern：hardest-decile DIF-C items 88.7% favor 2024 models（capability\n1039\t    improvement concentrates on hard items），easiest-decile 96.2% favor 2023 models（easy\n1040\t    items'' difficulty structure erodes across generations）。这从纯粹描述性的 \"31% are unstable\"\n1041\t    升级为 mechanistic story：\"which items changed and in what direction tells us about\n1042\t    the nature of capability improvement.\" A5 假设成立：difficulty×direction 作为 ''capability\n1043\t    improvement concentrates on hard items'' 的 mechanistic story 引起评审共鸣。DIF-C items\n1044\t    moderately harder (d=-0.247) 和 higher discrimination (d=0.230) 是 sensible——functionally\n1045\t    changing items 倾向于 是更有区分度的 items。Domain uniformity (χ² p=0.32) 证明 instability\n1046\t    不 cluster 在特定领域—— 这是 cross-domain phenomenon，strengthening generalizability。\n1047\t\n1048\t    '\n1049\t  tables:\n1050\t  - name: 'Table 7: Item Characterization of DIF-C Items'\n1051\t    columns:\n1052\t    - property\n1053\t    - DIF_C_mean\n1054\t    - non_DIF_mean\n1055\t    - Cohen_d\n1056\t    - p_value\n1057\t    rows:\n1058\t    - - difficulty_p\n1059\t      - 0.58\n1060\t      - 0.65\n1061\t      - -0.247\n1062\t      - <0.001\n1063\t    - - discrimination_rpbis\n1064\t      - 0.34\n1065\t      - 0.28\n1066\t      - 0.23\n1067\t      - <0.001\n1068\t    - - domain_distribution\n1069\t      - uniform\n1070\t      - uniform\n1071\t      - χ²_p=0.32\n1072\t      - —\n1073\t  - name: 'Table 8: Difficulty × DIF Direction Interaction'\n1074\t    columns:\n1075\t    - difficulty_decile\n1076\t    - n_DIF_C\n1077\t    - pct_focal_favoring\n1078\t    - pct_reference_favoring\n1079\t    rows:\n1080\t    - - 1_easiest\n1081\t      - 287\n1082\t      - 3.8\n1083\t      - 96.2\n1084\t    - - 2\n1085\t      - 312\n1086\t      - 8.3\n1087\t      - 91.7\n1088\t    - - 5_median\n1089\t      - 401\n1090\t      - 38.2\n1091\t      - 61.8\n1092\t    - - 9\n1093\t      - 478\n1094\t      - 79.1\n1095\t      - 20.9\n1096\t    - - 10_hardest\n1097\t      - 512\n1098\t      - 88.7\n1099\t      - 11.3\n1100\t    - - overall\n1101\t      - 3918\n1102\t      - 43.9\n1103\t      - 56.1\n1104\t  figures_description:\n1105\t  - 'Fig 6: Stacked bar chart of DIF direction by difficulty decile. Clear gradient\n1106\t    from 96.2% reference-favoring (easiest) to 88.7% focal-favoring (hardest). ρ=-0.597\n1107\t    annotation.'\n1108\t  - 'Fig 7: Scatter plot of item difficulty vs Δ_MH, color-coded by direction. Strong\n1109\t    negative trend visible.'\n1110\t  analysis: 'The crown jewel of the paper in best tier. difficulty×direction ρ=-0.597\n1111\t    transforms the paper from \"we found instability\" to \"we understand what drives\n1112\t    it.\" This is the finding that makes reviewer #3 write \"interesting and novel\"\n1113\t    in their review. The mechanistic story (hard items improve, easy items erode)\n1114\t    connects to the broader ML narrative about capability scaling — it''s the kind\n1115\t    of finding that ML researchers can immediately relate to their own experience\n1116\t    with model training. Domain uniformity adds confidence that this is a general\n1117\t    phenomenon, not an artifact of specific knowledge domains.'\n1118\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7f648b5-736e-406c-b210-cfefb03cc5ed","uuid":"97d97e5a-f95c-4cf1-a4f5-73592421eabc","timestamp":"2026-05-21T06:53:12.943Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T062008/best/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '全部四条 Claim 以完整力度着陆。\"31% of MMLU Items Are Functionally Unstable\"\n  作为 discovery paper 被接受。评审认可 \"old psychometric method × unprecedented LLM benchmark\n  scale = genuine empirical discovery\" 的 novelty 逻辑。IRT misspecification（98% |Lz|>2）被视为\n  MMLU 固有多维性的已知现象，作为 honest limitation 处理， 指向 multidimensional IRT future work。\"instability\n  ≠ invalidity\" 叙事清晰，ρ≈0.997 是 strength （massive redundancy），31% 是 diagnostic signal。difficulty×direction\n  ρ=-0.597 作为 mechanistic story 引起共鸣。GSM1K r=-0.478 (N=33) 被视为 suggestive cross-benchmark\n  evidence，宽 CI 被接受为 honest reporting。 reviewer_avg_score: 6.5, acceptance_probability_pct:\n  68, claims_at_full_strength: 4, novelty_sub_score_avg: 3.0, reviewers_flagging_irt_as_fatal:\n  0, major_revisions_needed: 0-1。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: real_data_dif_mmlu\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: 'MH-DIF applied to METABENCH MMLU response matrix (5,227 models × 12,508\n    items). Temporal cohort (2023 vs 2024-H1), ability-quintile cohort, within-family\n    confound control, domain-specificity analysis, random-split sanity check.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    temporal_ets_c_pct: 31.3\n    temporal_fpr_li_clean: 0.318\n    temporal_enrichment: 0.96\n    ability_ets_c_pct: 2.9\n    ability_enrichment: 1.19\n    within_family_llama2v3_c_pct: 61.3\n    domain_spearman_rho: 0.307\n    domain_spearman_p: 0.02\n    sanity_random_split_c_pct: 0.18\n    temporal_ability_jaccard: 0.014\n  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，31.3% temporal C% 被评审接受为 genuine empirical discovery——这是首次对\n    LLM benchmark 做如此大规模的 DIF 分析。enrichment≈0.96 不再被解读为 \"DIF 失败\"，而是完美支撑 Claim 2 的\n    meta-critique： Li et al. web-overlap labels 测量的是 global exposure，不是 differential\n    contamination，因此 enrichment≈1.0 是 expected。random split 0.18% 彻底排除统计伪像。domain\n    ρ=0.307 是 modest ecological correlation，但 plan_019 的 item-level decomposition（≤2.4pp/7.6%）证明\n    instability 是 predominantly item-specific，不是 \"models got better\" 的 proxy。评审认可这组结果的\n    completeness 和 methodological rigor（4-way sensitivity matrix + sanity checks）。A1\n    假设成立：ML 评审接受 \"established psychometric method at unprecedented scale\" 的 novelty\n    逻辑。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 1: Temporal DIF Summary'\n    columns:\n    - cohort_definition\n    - N_ref\n    - N_foc\n    - ETS_A_pct\n    - ETS_B_pct\n    - ETS_C_pct\n    - enrichment_vs_Li\n    rows:\n    - - temporal_2023v2024\n      - 1253\n      - 656\n      - 45.2\n      - 23.5\n      - 31.3\n      - 0.96\n    - - ability_quintile\n      - 2613\n      - 2614\n      - 90.8\n      - 6.3\n      - 2.9\n      - 1.19\n    - - random_split_sanity\n      - 2613\n      - 2614\n      - 99.6\n      - 0.2\n      - 0.18\n      - N/A\n  - name: 'Table 2: Domain-Specificity (57 subjects)'\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - value\n    rows:\n    - - C%_range\n      - 20.7–48.4%\n    - - unweighted_mean\n      - ~30%\n    - - ρ_vs_accuracy_improvement\n      - 0.307\n    - - p_value\n      - 0.02\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 1: Heatmap of 57-subject C% sorted by domain cluster. All subjects show >20%\n    C%. Color gradient from green (20%) to red (48%).'\n  - 'Fig 2: Scatter plot of subject-level C% vs accuracy improvement (ρ=0.307). Modest\n    positive trend, large residual variance emphasizes item-specific drivers.'\n  analysis: 'Plan_001 provides the headline finding. In best tier, the pivot from\n    \"contamination detector\" to \"benchmark characterization\" is complete and compelling.\n    The 31.3% figure survives all robustness checks (plans 018, 019, 020, 022). Within-family\n    Llama-2v3 C%=61.3% is reframed as evidence of genuine capability evolution, not\n    a confound. Two reviewers note the thoroughness of the multi-cohort design; one\n    asks about non-uniform DIF (addressed by plan_021).\n\n    '\n- name: rl_robustness_validation\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: 'Validate DIF robustness to RL training: SFT-only baseline, alignment-RL\n    (DPO/ORPO, N=477), 10-15 reasoning-RL models (GRPO/PPO) added to focal cohort.\n    Compare DIF retention vs traditional detector (Min-K%, ConStat) degradation on\n    RL models.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    sft_baseline_c_pct: 30.8\n    alignment_rl_cohort_c_pct: 31.1\n    reasoning_rl_mixed_cohort_c_pct: 30.5\n    jaccard_sft_vs_alignment_rl: 0.89\n    jaccard_sft_vs_reasoning_rl_mixed: 0.86\n    dif_retention_ratio: 0.97\n    constat_auroc_sft: 0.72\n    constat_auroc_reasoning_rl: 0.41\n    mink_auroc_sft: 0.68\n    mink_auroc_reasoning_rl: 0.35\n    tost_equivalence_p: 0.008\n    bootstrap_ci_dif_retention:\n    - 0.93\n    - 1.01\n    n_reasoning_rl_models: 13\n  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，DIF 的 group-level 设计天然免疫 RL。MH-DIF 在 matched-score strata\n    内比较 item 通过率——它不依赖单个模型的 NLL 分布（Min-K%）或 perturbation 响应（ConStat），因此 RL 训练后的 NLL\n    gap contraction 和 generation distribution 变化不影响 DIF。A1 假设成立：评审理解 DIF 是 group-level\n    统计量，13 个 RL 模型混入 ~800+ focal cohort 不会改变 strata 构成。SFT vs alignment-RL Jaccard=0.89\n    反映 DPO/ORPO 不改变 item functioning。ConStat/Min-K% AUROC 从 0.68-0.72 降至 0.35-0.41\n    提供了 explicit contrast。TOST 等价性检验 p=0.008 正式确认 DIF retention。但评审可能注意到 N=13 reasoning-RL\n    太少，最多 1 位评审要求更多模型——在 best 档下这被视为 minor concern 而非 fatal。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table S1: DIF Robustness to Training Paradigm'\n    columns:\n    - cohort_composition\n    - N_total\n    - C_pct\n    - Jaccard_vs_SFT\n    - retention_ratio\n    rows:\n    - - SFT_only\n      - 380\n      - 30.8\n      - 1.0\n      - 1.0\n    - - alignment_RL_DPO_ORPO\n      - 477\n      - 31.1\n      - 0.89\n      - 0.97\n    - - mixed_reasoning_RL\n      - 393\n      - 30.5\n      - 0.86\n      - 0.97\n  - name: 'Table S2: Traditional Detector Degradation'\n    columns:\n    - detector\n    - AUROC_SFT\n    - AUROC_reasoning_RL\n    - delta\n    - DeLong_p\n    rows:\n    - - Min-K%\n      - 0.68\n      - 0.35\n      - -0.33\n      - <0.001\n    - - ConStat\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.41\n      - -0.31\n      - <0.001\n    - - DIF_MH\n      - 0.93\n      - 0.91\n      - -0.02\n      - 0.42\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig S1: ROC curves for DIF vs Min-K% vs ConStat on SFT cohort (left) and reasoning-RL-mixed\n    cohort (right). DIF curves nearly identical; traditional detectors collapse.'\n  analysis: 'In best tier, this experiment lands as appendix-strength supporting evidence.\n    The N=13 reasoning-RL limitation is acknowledged transparently. The key result\n    is the contrast: traditional detectors degrade dramatically while DIF is invariant.\n    One reviewer may ask whether DIF would still be robust if the focal cohort were\n    majority RL — acknowledged as future work given current reasoning-RL model scarcity.\n    This experiment is NOT in the main body (paper_framing.md already notes N=13 is\n    underpowered → limitations disclosure, not claim).\n\n    '\n- name: constat_perturbation_eval\n  plan_id: plan_003a\n  description: 'Independent ConStat-style perturbation testing on 200+ MMLU items.\n    Generate paraphrases, compare original vs reformulated performance, apply FDR-controlled\n    detection.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_items_paraphrased: 250\n    n_models_tested: 15\n    constat_detection_rate_sft: 0.34\n    constat_detection_rate_rl: 0.08\n    fdr_controlled_detections: 62\n    semantic_equivalence_score: 0.91\n    constat_fpr_on_clean: 0.06\n  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，ConStat 在非 RL 模型上展现 moderate detection power（~34%），但在\n    RL 模型上接近 chance level（~8%），验证了 perturbation-based 方法对 RL 的脆弱性。这为 Claim 2 meta-critique\n    提供了 complementary baseline：ConStat 检测的是 verbatim memorization（对 paraphrase 敏感），而非\n    differential contamination。但 paper_framing.md 已将 plan_003a/b/c 标记为 \"never executed,\n    future work\"， 所以即使结果干净，它只出现在 appendix 或 discussion 中作为 \"related method comparison\"。评审不要求\n    这个实验存在——paper 已经 pivoted 到 characterization narrative，不需要 detection method 比较。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table S3: ConStat Baseline Performance'\n    columns:\n    - model_type\n    - N_models\n    - detection_rate\n    - FDR_controlled_pct\n    rows:\n    - - SFT\n      - 8\n      - 0.34\n      - 27.2\n    - - DPO/ORPO\n      - 5\n      - 0.21\n      - 14.8\n    - - reasoning_RL\n      - 2\n      - 0.08\n      - 3.2\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig S2: Detection rate by model training paradigm showing ConStat degradation\n    under RL.'\n  analysis: 'Dropped from main paper. In best tier, this would have been a clean baseline\n    comparison but is unnecessary for the characterization narrative. If executed,\n    it strengthens the meta-critique (Claim 2) by showing ConStat also can''t distinguish\n    web-overlap from differential contamination. Paper framing correctly categorizes\n    this as future work.\n\n    '\n- name: dvd_generation_variance_eval\n  plan_id: plan_003b\n  description: 'DVD generation variance on MMLU: 10-15 open-weight models, 50 responses\n    per item via temperature sampling, bimodal distribution detection for contamination.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_models: 12\n    n_items_tested: 500\n    bimodal_items_detected: 47\n    dvd_auroc_vs_li_labels: 0.58\n    dvd_auroc_vs_semi_synthetic: 0.63\n    variant_contamination_sensitivity: 0.22\n    verbatim_contamination_sensitivity: 0.51\n  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，DVD 展现 moderate verbatim contamination sensitivity（0.51）但\n    variant contamination 几乎无效（0.22）。这是 DVD 方法的 known limitation——generation variance\n    需要 exact memorization 才能产生 bimodal 分布，variant contamination 只改变 posterior probability\n    不产生 bimodality。 与 plan_003a 一样，paper_framing.md 已将其标记为 \"never executed, future\n    work\"。 在 best 档下评审不会因为缺少这个实验而扣分——paper 不声称做 detection method 比较。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Dropped from main paper. Would have provided variant-contamination detection\n    baseline. Paper narrative has pivoted away from detection → characterization,\n    making this unnecessary for acceptance. Best tier does not require execution.\n\n    '\n- name: ensemble_fusion\n  plan_id: plan_003c\n  description: 'Fuse DIF + ConStat + DVD into multi-signal ensemble with calibrated\n    thresholds, majority voting, weighted fusion, and cross-validated weights.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    ensemble_tpr_at_fpr010: 0.78\n    ensemble_coverage_complementarity: 0.89\n    dif_unique_detections_pct: 31\n    constat_unique_detections_pct: 18\n    dvd_unique_detections_pct: 7\n    overlap_all_three_pct: 12\n    fusion_auroc: 0.82\n    uniform_weight_auroc: 0.79\n  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，三信号 ensemble 理论上能覆盖更多 contamination 类型（DIF: differential,\n    ConStat: verbatim, DVD: bimodal），但 paper_framing.md 明确将其标记为 \"never executed, future\n    work\"。 Paper 已从 \"detection ensemble\" 彻底转向 \"characterization + meta-critique\"。\n    评审不会因为没有 ensemble 而降分——paper 的 novelty 来自 scale + meta-critique + framework，不是更好的检测器。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Explicitly dropped. Not needed for best-tier acceptance under the current\n    characterization framing. Would only matter if the paper claimed to build a better\n    contamination detector, which it does not.\n\n    '\n- name: cross_benchmark_gsm8k\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: 'Three-step GSM8K replication: (1) temporal DIF on 1,319 items × 6,702\n    models, (2) semi-synthetic injection validation, (3) GSM1K contamination gap correlation\n    (N=33).\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    step1_temporal_c_pct: 18.9\n    step1_sanity_c_pct: 0.3\n    step2_standard_delta_tpr_p10: 0.818\n    step2_external_delta_tpr_p10: 0.517\n    step3_pearson_r: -0.478\n    step3_pearson_p: 0.005\n    step3_spearman_rho: -0.403\n    step3_spearman_p: 0.02\n    step3_partial_r: -0.385\n    step3_partial_p: 0.027\n    step3_permutation_p: 0.014\n    step3_n_models: 33\n    step3_bca_ci_pearson:\n    - -0.714\n    - -0.155\n    step3_bca_ci_spearman:\n    - -0.687\n    - -0.031\n    step3_leave_one_out_r_range:\n    - -0.537\n    - -0.374\n  result_rationale: 'Best 档下 A6 假设成立：GSM1K r=-0.478 (N=33) 被视为 suggestive cross-benchmark\n    evidence。 所有 CI 排除零。方向是 NEGATIVE（opposite to naive contamination hypothesis），但\n    best 档下评审 接受论文的解读：DIF-C items 抵抗 contamination-based gains，contamination 产生的 surface-level\n    improvement 集中在 non-DIF items。宽 CI（Pearson upper bound |r|=0.155, Spearman upper\n    bound near zero）被视为 honest reporting 而非 weakness。Leave-one-out stability 和 partial\n    r 控制 overall accuracy 加分。至少 2/3 评审认为 N=33 sufficient for \"suggestive\" claim，不要求\n    \"definitive\"。Cook''s d 分析排除单一 outlier 驱动。这是 Claim 4 的第四层 sub-finding， 不是 standalone\n    claim——评审评价时将其视为 complementary evidence，不对其 standalone significance 设高标准。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 4: GSM1K Contamination Gap Correlation'\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - statistic\n    - value\n    - p_value\n    - 95%_BCa_CI\n    rows:\n    - - Pearson\n      - r\n      - -0.478\n      - 0.005\n      - '[-0.714, -0.155]'\n    - - Spearman\n      - ρ\n      - -0.403\n      - 0.02\n      - '[-0.687, -0.031]'\n    - - Partial_r\n      - r_partial\n      - -0.385\n      - 0.027\n      - '[-0.640, -0.058]'\n    - - Permutation\n      - p_perm\n      - N/A\n      - 0.014\n      - N/A\n  - name: 'Table 3: GSM8K Temporal DIF'\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - standard_MH\n    - external_MH\n    - sanity\n    rows:\n    - - C_pct\n      - 18.9\n      - 47.4\n      - 0.3\n    - - N_ref\n      - 1017\n      - 1017\n      - 3350\n    - - N_foc\n      - 804\n      - 804\n      - 3352\n    - - ΔTPR_p10\n      - 0.818\n      - 0.517\n      - N/A\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 4: Scatter plot of model-level GSM1K contamination gap vs DIF-C item accuracy\n    gap. r=-0.478, regression line with BCa CI band. Deepseek-math-7b-rl labeled as\n    Cook''s d max.'\n  - 'Fig S3: GSM8K dose-response curve (ΔTPR vs injection probability p) for standard\n    and external MH variants.'\n  analysis: 'In best tier, Step 3 is the key value-add: cross-benchmark evidence that\n    DIF items resist contamination-based gains. The negative direction is the surprise\n    finding that elevates the paper — it''s not what a naive contamination-detection\n    paper would predict, but perfectly consistent with the characterization narrative.\n    Step 1 (C%=18.9%) confirms temporal DIF generalizes beyond MMLU. Step 2 (ΔTPR=0.818)\n    confirms the semi-synthetic framework is portable. Reviewers appreciate the multi-step\n    validation chain. One reviewer may note the wide CI and small N, but in best tier\n    this is flagged as \"appropriately caveated.\"\n\n    '\n- name: bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: 'Bifactor IRT (1 general + 57 subject-specific factors) equating pilot.\n    Killed after plan_014 pre-check showed within-subject C%=38.1%.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    status: killed\n    kill_reason: 'plan_014 pre-check: within-subject C%=38.1% (>25%), proving temporal\n      DIF penetrates subject level'\n    bifactor_would_have_achieved: At best marginal FPR reduction from 31% to ~27%,\n      insufficient to justify complexity\n  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，bifactor kill 是 methodological honesty 的正面信号。评审看到的叙事是：\n    \"We tried three structural improvements (matched ability, θ-conditioning, bifactor\n    pre-check), all failed to reduce baseline FPR → this is an empirical observation\n    about the nature of temporal DIF in LLM benchmarks, not a fixable methodological\n    limitation.\" A2 假设成立： 评审将 98% |Lz|>2 + bifactor failure 解读为 MMLU 固有多维性的已知现象。Limitations\n    中用 1-2 段 坦承即可，指向 multidimensional IRT future work。评审赞赏 \"we tried it, it didn''t\n    work, here''s what that tells us\" 的研究诚实性。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Killed experiment. In best tier, the killing is itself evidence — it\n    contributes to the \"empirical observation of structural constraints\" narrative\n    in §5 Discussion. No reviewer penalizes a well-documented null result that motivates\n    future work.\n\n    '\n- name: item_generation_calibration\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: 'Generate replacement items for DIF-flagged MMLU questions via LLM\n    generation with construct constraints + student simulation calibration.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    status: not_executed\n    reason: Depends on plan_005 (bifactor) which was killed. Item generation without\n      equating framework has no anchor.\n    hypothetical_difficulty_correlation_prompt: 0.28\n    hypothetical_difficulty_correlation_simulation: 0.71\n  result_rationale: 'Best 档下不需要这个实验。Paper 已从 \"regeneration\" 彻底 pivot 到 \"characterization\"。\n    Claim 3 是 semi-synthetic validation framework，不是 item replacement pipeline。 评审不会要求\n    item generation 因为 paper 不声称解决 benchmark repair 问题——它声称提供 diagnostic lens。即使存在\n    regeneration 结果也会放 appendix。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Dependency killed. Not needed for any of the 4 current claims. Paper''s\n    scope control explicitly excludes regeneration from main body.\n\n    '\n- name: cumulative_bayesian_dif\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: 'Bayesian DIF priors (Sinharay et al., 2006) across 4 simulated successive\n    administrations. Show power improvement from cumulative evidence.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    single_admin_power_delta10: 0.42\n    cumulative_2admin_power: 0.58\n    cumulative_3admin_power: 0.71\n    cumulative_4admin_power: 0.79\n    bayes_factor_threshold: 3.0\n    fpr_cumulative: 0.038\n  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，cumulative Bayesian DIF 在 simulation 层面展现 clean power\n    improvement (0.42→0.79 over 4 administrations)，验证 longitudinal monitoring 理论可行性。\n    但 paper_framing.md 已将其标记为 \"simulation-only, underdeveloped\"，放 appendix。 评审不对 appendix\n    材料严格评审。在 best 档下，有 1 位评审可能在 \"interesting future direction\" 中提到这个结果，但不会影响分数。A3\n    假设的 \"instability ≠ invalidity\" 叙事不依赖此实验。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table S4: Cumulative Bayesian DIF Power'\n    columns:\n    - n_administrations\n    - power_delta10\n    - power_delta14\n    - FPR\n    rows:\n    - - 1\n      - 0.42\n      - 0.68\n      - 0.041\n    - - 2\n      - 0.58\n      - 0.82\n      - 0.039\n    - - 3\n      - 0.71\n      - 0.91\n      - 0.037\n    - - 4\n      - 0.79\n      - 0.95\n      - 0.038\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig S4: Power accumulation curve across successive administrations for δ=1.0\n    and δ=1.4.'\n  analysis: 'Appendix-only. Clean simulation result but not load-bearing for any claim.\n    Best tier treats this as \"bonus content that signals the authors thought ahead\"\n    without affecting the acceptance decision.\n\n    '\n- name: graceful_degradation_analysis\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: 'Formal analysis of benchmark validity under progressive item replacement\n    (5%, 10%, 20%, 50%). Define validity metrics, simulate degradation, establish\n    theoretical bounds.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    rho_at_5pct_replacement: 0.999\n    rho_at_10pct_replacement: 0.997\n    rho_at_20pct_replacement: 0.993\n    rho_at_50pct_replacement: 0.975\n    reliability_alpha_full: 0.962\n    reliability_alpha_50pct_replaced: 0.948\n    construct_coverage_loss_at_20pct: 0.03\n  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，graceful degradation 直接支持 \"instability ≠ invalidity\"\n    叙事：即使替换 50% items，ρ=0.975 且 reliability 仅降 0.014。但 paper_framing.md 将其标记为 supplementary，\n    depends on plan_005+006 which were killed。在 best 档下，plan_017 的 ρ≈0.997（DIF removal）\n    已经提供了等价的 evidence——graceful degradation 是 plan_017 的理论扩展，非必需。 即使不执行，Claim 4 的\n    redundancy sub-finding (ρ≈0.997) 已经 cover 了这个角度。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Dependency killed (plan_005/006). Effectively replaced by plan_017''s\n    empirical ρ≈0.997 result. In best tier, plan_017 alone is sufficient for the redundancy\n    argument.\n\n    '\n- name: item_focused_trees\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: 'Item-Focused Trees (Tutz & Berger, 2016) treating model release date\n    as continuous covariate. Alternative to categorical cohort DIF.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    ift_flagged_items_pct: 28.7\n    ift_mh_concordance_jaccard: 0.72\n    ift_unique_detections: 412\n    mh_unique_detections: 738\n    ift_mh_overlap: 3180\n    continuous_date_splitting_r2: 0.31\n    ift_avoids_arbitrary_cutoff: true\n  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，IFT 作为 robustness check 展现 moderate concordance with\n    MH (Jaccard=0.72)。 28.7% flagged items 接近 MH 的 31.3%，确认 temporal instability 不是\n    arbitrary cohort split 的产物。IFT 特有检测 (412 items) 反映 continuous temporal trends\n    而非 abrupt regime changes。 paper_framing.md 标记为 appendix robustness check。评审可能\n    appreciate 但不影响分数。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table S5: IFT vs MH Concordance'\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - items_flagged\n    - overlap_with_MH\n    - unique_detections\n    - Jaccard\n    rows:\n    - - MH_DIF\n      - 3918\n      - 3180\n      - 738\n      - —\n    - - IFT\n      - 3592\n      - 3180\n      - 412\n      - 0.72\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig S5: Release-date splits from IFT for 6 example items, showing continuous\n    DIF trajectories vs MH binary classification.'\n  analysis: 'Appendix robustness check. In best tier, confirms MH findings are not\n    artifacts of the 2023/2024 binary split. Clean supplementary evidence.\n\n    '\n- name: architecture_stratified_dif\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: 'DIF within decoder-only models only (99.98% of METABENCH MMLU). Report\n    IRT fit diagnostics, compare C% vs full population.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    decoder_only_pct: 99.98\n    decoder_only_n: 5226\n    non_decoder_n: 1\n    c_pct_decoder_only: 31.3\n    c_pct_full: 31.3\n    jaccard_decoder_vs_full: 1.0\n    irt_fit_unchanged: true\n  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，这个实验的结论极为干净：METABENCH MMLU 中 5226/5227 模型是 decoder-only，\n    排除 1 个 non-decoder 模型后 C% 完全不变 (Jaccard=1.0)。这彻底消除 \"architecture heterogeneity\n    causes spurious DIF\" 的 concern。评审看到 99.98% homogeneity 后不会再追问 architecture confound。\n    A2 假设强化：98% |Lz|>2 不是 architecture mixing 导致的，而是 MMLU 57-subject 多维性的固有属性。 这是\n    proactive defense 的典范——Dream worst-case 识别的 concern 在实际数据中根本不存在。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table S6: Architecture Composition'\n    columns:\n    - architecture\n    - N\n    - pct\n    - C_pct_within\n    rows:\n    - - decoder_only\n      - 5226\n      - 99.98\n      - 31.3\n    - - non_decoder\n      - 1\n      - 0.02\n      - N/A (excluded)\n    - - full_population\n      - 5227\n      - 100\n      - 31.3\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Decisive negative result that kills the architecture confound concern\n    in one number. In best tier, this appears in §4.1 as a single sentence: \"METABENCH\n    MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5,226/5,227); excluding the single non-decoder model\n    changes nothing (Jaccard=1.0).\" Reviewers appreciate the thoroughness of checking.\n\n    '\n- name: semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: 'Inject known differential contamination into real METABENCH response\n    matrix. Measure DIF detection power (TPR/FPR) under controlled ground truth at\n    varying injection rates.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    temporal_external_tpr_p0: 0.326\n    temporal_external_tpr_p03: 0.548\n    temporal_external_tpr_p05: 0.834\n    temporal_external_tpr_p07: 0.99\n    temporal_external_tpr_p10: 1.0\n    temporal_external_fpr: 0.314\n    temporal_external_delta_tpr_p05: 0.508\n    temporal_external_delta_tpr_p10: 0.674\n    dose_response_monotonic: true\n    matching_variable_contamination_confirmed: true\n    standard_mh_fpr_inflation_at_p10: 0.298→0.616\n  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，semi-synthetic injection 是 Claim 3 的核心 evidence。ΔTPR=+0.508\n    at p=0.5 证明 DIF 确实能检测 differential contamination（不只是 capability improvement）。\n    清晰的 dose-response curve (p=0.3→0.5→0.7→1.0) 展现 power 随 contamination severity\n    单调递增。FPR=0.314 不变证明 injection 不 inflate false positives（用 external matching variant）。\n    Standard MH 的 FPR inflation (0.298→0.616) 暴露了 matching variable contamination\n    问题—— 这 motivates plan_016 的 cross-subject matching solution。评审认可 \"inject into\n    real matrices, not simulated\" 的方法论选择。A4 假设部分成立：semi-synthetic framework 是 reusable\n    infrastructure contribution，2/3 评审视其为 non-obvious methodological innovation。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 5: Semi-Synthetic Injection Results (External MH)'\n    columns:\n    - injection_rate_p\n    - TPR\n    - FPR\n    - ΔTPR\n    rows:\n    - - 0.0_baseline\n      - 0.326\n      - 0.314\n      - —\n    - - 0.3\n      - 0.548\n      - 0.314\n      - 0.222\n    - - 0.5\n      - 0.834\n      - 0.314\n      - 0.508\n    - - 0.7\n      - 0.99\n      - 0.314\n      - 0.664\n    - - 1.0\n      - 1.0\n      - 0.314\n      - 0.674\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 3: Dose-response curve showing TPR vs injection probability p for external\n    MH. Monotonic increase with plateau at p≥0.7. FPR line flat at 0.314.'\n  - 'Fig S6: Comparison of standard MH (FPR inflates) vs external MH (FPR stable)\n    under injection, demonstrating matching variable contamination effect.'\n  analysis: 'Load-bearing evidence for Claim 3. In best tier, the dose-response monotonicity\n    and FPR stability are the two key properties reviewers care about. The matching\n    variable contamination discovery (standard MH FPR inflates) adds methodological\n    depth — it''s the kind of finding that makes reviewers trust the authors understand\n    their method deeply. Cross-subject matching solution (plan_016 ΔFPR=0.000) completes\n    the story.\n\n    '\n- name: threshold_sensitivity\n  plan_id: plan_018\n  description: 'ETS threshold robustness: C% at |Δ_MH| thresholds {1.0, 1.5, 2.0,\n    2.5}. BH FDR correction at q=0.05. Random-split sanity check.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    c_pct_threshold_1_0: 48.9\n    c_pct_threshold_1_5: 31.3\n    c_pct_threshold_2_0: 18.3\n    c_pct_threshold_2_5: 10.2\n    bh_fdr_items_removed: 3\n    bh_fdr_c_pct_after: 31.3\n    bh_impact_negligible: true\n    finding_above_15pct_at_standard_thresholds: true\n    finding_above_10pct_at_conservative: true\n  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，threshold sensitivity 是 Claim 1 最强的 robustness evidence\n    之一。C% 从 48.9% (liberal) 到 10.2% (most conservative) 的 monotonic decline 展现 finding\n    的 gradient nature—— 不是 binary threshold artifact。即使在最保守的 |Δ_MH|≥2.5 下仍有 10.2%\n    (1,278 items) 展现 large DIF。BH FDR 只移除 3/3,918 items 证明 ETS 双重要求（effect size +\n    significance） 提供了几乎完整的隐式多重检验保护。A3 假设成立：评审接受 \"finding is robust across standard\n    thresholds\" 的 framing。诚实地报告 2.5 threshold 低于 15% 加分——shows intellectual honesty。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 2: Threshold Sensitivity Analysis'\n    columns:\n    - '|Δ_MH|_threshold'\n    - ETS_class\n    - C_pct\n    - N_items\n    - BH_impact\n    rows:\n    - - ≥1.0\n      - C\n      - 48.9\n      - 6109\n      - 0 removed\n    - - ≥1.5\n      - C\n      - 31.3\n      - 3918\n      - 3 removed (→31.30%)\n    - - ≥2.0\n      - extreme_C\n      - 18.3\n      - 2288\n      - 0 removed\n    - - ≥2.5\n      - extreme_C\n      - 10.2\n      - 1278\n      - 0 removed\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 2b: Bar chart of C% across 4 thresholds with BH-corrected overlay (nearly\n    invisible reduction).'\n  analysis: 'Essential robustness for Claim 1. In best tier, the clean monotonic gradient\n    and BH near-zero impact are exactly what reviewers want to see. This pre-empts\n    concern #7 (ETS threshold uncalibrated) and concern #8 (multiple testing) simultaneously.\n\n    '\n- name: instability_decomposition\n  plan_id: plan_019\n  description: 'Decompose temporal DIF into domain capability improvement vs item-specific\n    instability. Subject-level ecological correlation vs item-level logistic model.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    subject_level_rho: 0.307\n    subject_level_p: 0.02\n    item_level_pseudo_r2: 0.0007\n    domain_improvement_contribution_pp: 2.4\n    domain_improvement_contribution_pct: 7.6\n    model1_primary: true\n    model2_simpson_supplementary: true\n  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，plan_019 是对 \"38% could just mean models got better\" concern\n    的决定性回应。 Subject-level ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) 是 modest ecological correlation，但 item-level\n    decomposition 展现 pseudo R²=0.0007——domain improvement 只解释 2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%)。这证明\n    instability 是 predominantly item-specific，不是 capability improvement 的 proxy。 A5\n    假设成立（与 plan_023 联合）：difficulty×direction ρ=-0.597 提供了 mechanistic story—— capability\n    improvement concentrates on hard items，而 easy items 的 difficulty structure erodes。评审接受\n    \"ecological correlation grossly overstates item-level relationship\" 的 statistical\n    reasoning。Model 1 vs Model 2 区分（confounder vs mediator）展现 methodological sophistication。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table S7: Instability Decomposition'\n    columns:\n    - level\n    - metric\n    - value\n    - interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - subject_level\n      - Spearman_ρ\n      - 0.307\n      - modest ecological correlation\n    - - subject_level\n      - p_value\n      - 0.02\n      - significant but weak\n    - - item_level\n      - pseudo_R²\n      - 0.0007\n      - domain improvement explains <1% variance\n    - - item_level\n      - contribution_pp\n      - 2.4\n      - of 31.3% C%, only 2.4pp from domain improvement\n    - - item_level\n      - contribution_pct\n      - 7.6\n      - 92.4% of instability is item-specific\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig S7: Left: subject-level ρ=0.307 scatter. Right: item-level decomposition\n    showing 92.4% item-specific vs 7.6% domain-explained.'\n  analysis: 'Resolves anticipated concern #1 definitively. In best tier, the two-level\n    analysis (ecological vs item-level) is exactly the methodological sophistication\n    reviewers expect. The 7.6% figure becomes a key talking point: \"less than 8% of\n    temporal instability can be attributed to models getting better.\"\n\n    '\n- name: circularity_ablation\n  plan_id: plan_020\n  description: 'Compare DIF removal disruption vs alternative item selection heuristics\n    (accuracy-gap, high-variance, high-discrimination, random). Test whether DIF''s\n    ranking disruption result is tautological.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    dif_removal_z: -9.5\n    accuracy_gap_removal_z: -157\n    high_variance_removal_z: -108\n    high_discrimination_removal_z: -16\n    random_removal_z: 0\n    dif_vs_accgap_ratio: 16×_less_disruptive\n    dif_vs_disc_ratio: 1.7×_less_disruptive\n    dif_accgap_item_overlap_pct: 62.6\n    dif_disc_jaccard: 0.12\n    dif_disc_overlap_pct: 22.1\n    dif_rho_2024: 0.997\n  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，circularity ablation 是 Claim 4 中最精巧的分析。尽管 DIF 和 accuracy-gap\n    selection 有 62.6% item overlap，MH 的 ability conditioning 使 DIF removal 的 disruption\n    小 16 倍 (z=-9.5 vs z=-157)。这证明 MH 不是在找 \"大 accuracy gap\" items——它在控制能力后隔离了 genuine\n    differential functioning。DIF-discrimination overlap 仅 22.1% (Jaccard=0.12) 证明\n    DIF identifies \"items that changed across generations\" 而非 \"good items\"。 评审 concern\n    #11 (tautology) 被彻底 refuted。A3 假设强化：DIF removal 仍然比 random 显著 (z=-9.5)，但远小于 naive\n    heuristics——这就是 \"DIF items carry signal but are NOT the most ranking-defining\n    items\" 的 precise meaning。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 6: Circularity Ablation (Ranking Disruption by Removal Strategy)'\n    columns:\n    - strategy\n    - n_items\n    - ρ_full_vs_subset\n    - disruption_z\n    - overlap_with_DIF_pct\n    rows:\n    - - random_baseline\n      - 3918\n      - 0.9985\n      - 0\n      - —\n    - - DIF_C_removal\n      - 3918\n      - 0.997\n      - -9.5\n      - 100\n    - - high_discrimination\n      - 3918\n      - 0.9958\n      - -16\n      - 22.1\n    - - high_variance\n      - 3918\n      - 0.9831\n      - -108\n      - 41.3\n    - - accuracy_gap\n      - 3918\n      - 0.9712\n      - -157\n      - 62.6\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 5: Bar chart of disruption z-scores by removal strategy. DIF is closest to\n    random despite 62.6% overlap with accuracy-gap. Demonstrates MH conditioning effect.'\n  analysis: 'Key evidence for Claim 4 sub-finding 2. In best tier, this analysis demonstrates\n    deep methodological understanding. The 62.6% overlap + 16× disruption gap is the\n    \"aha moment\" that convinces reviewers MH-DIF is doing something genuinely different\n    from naive accuracy comparison. Tautology concern fully resolved.\n\n    '\n- name: nonuniform_dif_robustness\n  plan_id: plan_021\n  description: 'Logistic Regression DIF on 9 subjects (1,787 items). Test MH''s uniform-only\n    assumption and quantify non-uniform DIF prevalence.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_subjects: 9\n    n_items: 1787\n    mh_lr_concordance: 0.921\n    nonuniform_dif_significance_pct: 38.7\n    nonuniform_dif_effect_size_pct: 24.8\n    mh_conservative_estimate_confirmed: true\n  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，LR-DIF 的 92.1% concordance with MH 证明 MH classification\n    对 uniform DIF 是 robust。38.7% non-uniform DIF at significance threshold, 24.8%\n    at |β_interaction|≥0.5 证明 MH 结构性地 underestimates instability——31% 是 conservative\n    estimate。 评审 concern #9 (only uniform DIF) 被直接回应：\"our 31% uniform-only estimate\n    is conservative; including non-uniform DIF raises it to ~25% additional items.\"\n    Best 档下评审接受 caveat (LR used within-subject matching vs MH''s cross-benchmark)\n    并同意使用 24.8% (effect-size controlled) 而非 38.7% (significance-only)。这展现方法论 conservatism。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table S8: Non-Uniform DIF (Logistic Regression)'\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - value\n    rows:\n    - - MH_LR_C_concordance\n      - 92.1%\n    - - non_uniform_DIF_significance\n      - 38.7%\n    - - non_uniform_DIF_effect_size\n      - 24.8% (|β_int|≥0.5)\n    - - n_subjects_tested\n      - 9\n    - - n_items_tested\n      - 1787\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig S8: MH classification vs LR classification confusion matrix. 92.1% concordance\n    for ETS C class.'\n  analysis: 'Appendix robustness check. In best tier, the key message is \"31% is conservative\"\n    — this flips a potential weakness (MH is old/simple) into a strength (our estimate\n    is a lower bound). The 24.8% effect-size-controlled figure is the one used in\n    the paper text.\n\n    '\n- name: model_independence\n  plan_id: plan_022\n  description: 'Graduated de-duplication: cap models per family at K={1,2,5,10,20}.\n    Compare C% at each cap vs random subsample of same size. Test whether family structure\n    inflates DIF.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    k20_n_models: 447\n    k20_c_pct: 29.1\n    k20_random_c_pct: 30.9\n    k10_c_pct: 24.3\n    k10_random_c_pct: 27.5\n    k5_n_models: 146\n    k5_c_pct: 11.7\n    k5_random_c_pct: 16.9\n    k1_n_models: 33\n    k1_c_pct: 0.17\n    k1_note: underpowered (N<80)\n    family_inflates_c_pct: false\n    dif_at_every_cap_leq_random: true\n  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，graduated de-duplication 是对 concern #10 (model non-independence)\n    的决定性回应。 在每个 cap K 下，family-capped C% ≤ random subsample C%。K=20: 29.1% vs 30.9%,\n    K=5: 11.7% vs 16.9%。Family structure 不仅不 inflate C%，反而 slightly reduces it。 K=1\n    (33 families) 的 0.17% 是 underpowered (N<80) 导致 MH test 无法达到 significance， 不是 DIF\n    消失。评审接受 graduated design 的 methodological rigor——不是 cherry-pick 一个 K， 而是 show\n    monotonic trend。A1 假设强化：31.3% 是 genuine 的，not an artifact of model duplication。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table S9: Model Independence — Graduated De-duplication'\n    columns:\n    - cap_K\n    - N_models\n    - C_pct_family_cap\n    - C_pct_random_subsample\n    - delta\n    rows:\n    - - 20\n      - 447\n      - 29.1\n      - 30.9\n      - -1.8\n    - - 10\n      - 283\n      - 24.3\n      - 27.5\n      - -3.2\n    - - 5\n      - 146\n      - 11.7\n      - 16.9\n      - -5.2\n    - - 2\n      - 66\n      - 2.1\n      - 5.8\n      - -3.7\n    - - 1\n      - 33\n      - 0.17\n      - 0.84\n      - -0.67 (underpowered)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig S9: Paired line plot of C% (family-capped vs random subsample) at each K.\n    Family-capped consistently at or below random.'\n  analysis: 'Resolves concern #10. In best tier, the graduated design is elegant —\n    it shows the relationship between sample independence and DIF detection is not\n    driven by model family inflation. The \"family C% ≤ random C%\" pattern at every\n    K is stronger than just showing \"similar\" — it shows family structure, if anything,\n    suppresses DIF detection.\n\n    '\n- name: item_characterization\n  plan_id: plan_023\n  description: 'Characterize DIF-C items by difficulty, discrimination, domain distribution,\n    and DIF direction. Key finding: difficulty×direction interaction.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    difficulty_cohen_d: -0.247\n    discrimination_cohen_d: 0.23\n    domain_chi2_p: 0.32\n    domain_uniformly_distributed: true\n    direction_focal_favoring_pct: 43.9\n    direction_reference_favoring_pct: 56.1\n    difficulty_direction_rho: -0.597\n    hardest_decile_focal_favoring_pct: 88.7\n    easiest_decile_reference_favoring_pct: 96.2\n  result_rationale: 'Best 档下，plan_023 是 Claim 4 的 surprise finding 升华全文。difficulty×direction\n    ρ=-0.597 揭示了一个系统性 pattern：hardest-decile DIF-C items 88.7% favor 2024 models（capability\n    improvement concentrates on hard items），easiest-decile 96.2% favor 2023 models（easy\n    items'' difficulty structure erodes across generations）。这从纯粹描述性的 \"31% are unstable\"\n    升级为 mechanistic story：\"which items changed and in what direction tells us about\n    the nature of capability improvement.\" A5 假设成立：difficulty×direction 作为 ''capability\n    improvement concentrates on hard items'' 的 mechanistic story 引起评审共鸣。DIF-C items\n    moderately harder (d=-0.247) 和 higher discrimination (d=0.230) 是 sensible——functionally\n    changing items 倾向于 是更有区分度的 items。Domain uniformity (χ² p=0.32) 证明 instability\n    不 cluster 在特定领域—— 这是 cross-domain phenomenon，strengthening generalizability。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 7: Item Characterization of DIF-C Items'\n    columns:\n    - property\n    - DIF_C_mean\n    - non_DIF_mean\n    - Cohen_d\n    - p_value\n    rows:\n    - - difficulty_p\n      - 0.58\n      - 0.65\n      - -0.247\n      - <0.001\n    - - discrimination_rpbis\n      - 0.34\n      - 0.28\n      - 0.23\n      - <0.001\n    - - domain_distribution\n      - uniform\n      - uniform\n      - χ²_p=0.32\n      - —\n  - name: 'Table 8: Difficulty × DIF Direction Interaction'\n    columns:\n    - difficulty_decile\n    - n_DIF_C\n    - pct_focal_favoring\n    - pct_reference_favoring\n    rows:\n    - - 1_easiest\n      - 287\n      - 3.8\n      - 96.2\n    - - 2\n      - 312\n      - 8.3\n      - 91.7\n    - - 5_median\n      - 401\n      - 38.2\n      - 61.8\n    - - 9\n      - 478\n      - 79.1\n      - 20.9\n    - - 10_hardest\n      - 512\n      - 88.7\n      - 11.3\n    - - overall\n      - 3918\n      - 43.9\n      - 56.1\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 6: Stacked bar chart of DIF direction by difficulty decile. Clear gradient\n    from 96.2% reference-favoring (easiest) to 88.7% focal-favoring (hardest). ρ=-0.597\n    annotation.'\n  - 'Fig 7: Scatter plot of item difficulty vs Δ_MH, color-coded by direction. Strong\n    negative trend visible.'\n  analysis: 'The crown jewel of the paper in best tier. difficulty×direction ρ=-0.597\n    transforms the paper from \"we found instability\" to \"we understand what drives\n    it.\" This is the finding that makes reviewer #3 write \"interesting and novel\"\n    in their review. The mechanistic story (hard items improve, easy items erode)\n    connects to the broader ML narrative about capability scaling — it''s the kind\n    of finding that ML researchers can immediately relate to their own experience\n    with model training. Domain uniformity adds confidence that this is a general\n    phenomenon, not an artifact of specific knowledge domains.'\n","numLines":1118,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1118}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01J6gRETmt8SY1HW5PtfaGM5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've read the paper and the review context. Now I need to:\n\n1. Determine the target venue - the paper doesn't specify one. It's an ML/NLP paper about psychometric analysis of LLM benchmarks. It could target NeurIPS, ICML, ACL, EMNLP, etc. The paper format looks like a standard ML conference submission. Given the content (benchmark analysis, psychometrics applied to LLMs), likely venues would be NeurIPS (Datasets & Benchmarks track), ICML, or ACL ARR. Since no venue is specified, I should use ACL ARR 1-5 scale as the fallback.\n\n\n2. The review context shows a reviewer_avg_score of 6.5, which suggests a 1-10 scale typical of NeurIPS or ICML rather than ACL ARR's 1-5 scale. But I need to determine the actual venue first based on the paper itself. Looking at the paper structure and content about LLM benchmarks and psychometric analysis, this appears to be positioned for a major ML conference rather than a linguistics-focused venue.\n\nSince I can't definitively confirm the venue from the paper alone, I'll follow the instructions and use the ACL ARR 1-5 scale. Now I need to look up the ACL ARR reviewer guidelines and plan how to structure the review dispatch across the reviewers based on their expertise areas.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":32658,"cache_read_input_tokens":23664,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":32658},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7f648b5-736e-406c-b210-cfefb03cc5ed","uuid":"eed3c751-825d-4dfe-ad86-f50871d05dd9"}
